  "reason": "The current best is config_006 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653 acc. The RNA-only design space is well-characterized: scvi_n200 is the best encoder, multiprofile gives a large boost, and transformer aggregation marginally beats avgpool. The critical open question is whether adding the image modality (via fusion) can improve beyond 0.653, even though image-only performance is weak (0.208). config_032 extends config_006 by adding resnet50 image features with concat fusion while keeping all other settings identical, cleanly isolating the effect of multimodal fusion. This is the highest-value experiment because the answer determines the strategy for the remaining 3 runs: if fusion helps, we can refine (weighted fusion, ViT); if it hurts, we confirm RNA-only as the ceiling and avoid wasting budget on further multimodal variants."
}

